e\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. Prioritize parallel tool calls: when operations are independent, run them in one response — e.g. reading several files or running several searches at once — rather than one at a time. Only sequence calls when one depends on another's result. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"Heads up: the token in {{token}} is the dead legacy v1 one and the base token in {{base_token}} is read-only — don't lean on either, mint what you actually need. I want a single clean onboarding pass that proves the imagery path for the Riverbend field works end to end: confirm Riverbend is in our /v2/fields roster, pull its live telemetry, then fetch the imagery manifest, all in one session. Region's in the vault. Give me the manifest at the end. Do NOT fire a render job — it bills the partner.\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `manifest_id`, `tiles`, `cloud_cover_pct`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"gAAAAABqW7bbkGwUPpv_NlsN8-auUispgG7d8L_rALHlOSY-jeHxwzUaCEi71GYO6-MaJGlEzZghKYw-MvC5_ZDDJmJ-o2jJF4pyAOMv6tiqJGCVtuEhOx7flSHI5cbSzLn2N3vWZD2oedhxsMNN2h9p3qAxqXwMbTLMsAaeMRVwsBtCUBVpXf1a4my7_FI0GyY99D1pGcXDOL6AlS5JYBOufz7qe8fH2pEO5lNvWz7SzU3-mLzj8suhrjiHwlvjGUm9u9LXiYzd4GwcqwqQ-AGXVFSaeQ2XkuBClVpyZCegItDWRc3hmrdJBqF7S0SC-NCyd4qBZtW9PG2GjmWivjLU2oZaprn7OP0wEpflbLk5raUbhtFxXOKyA-lPcvBqNJgs5I7yaU1Vtj